# Copy this to `.env` and fill in the value below.
#
# The GitHub OAuth app client id. This is PUBLIC by design — the app uses the
# OAuth device flow, which has no client secret. It is safe to commit, but it
# lives here (not hard-coded) so each fork uses its own OAuth app.
#
# To get one:
#   1. github.com -> Settings -> Developer settings -> OAuth Apps -> New
#   2. Enable "Device Flow".
#   3. Copy the Client ID here.
#
# See README.md, "Register a GitHub OAuth app".
EXPO_PUBLIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
